  "description": "The language algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines: number conversion (Number::toString at every radix, toFixed, toExponential, toPrecision, StringToNumber, parseInt, parseFloat, numeric literal values, numeric keys and the string white-space set), numerics (the integer conversions, Float16, the Math kernels, exact rounding and the BigInt kernel) and text (UTF-16, padding and relative indices, replacement templates, the URI, base64 and hex codecs, and JSON's grammar, quoting and gap), with the WorkCharge metering delegate, the ResultStatus enumeration and the limit records every shared operation uses.",
